{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Remember. And come to your senses.</b> Some say it is like והוסדו, like אשיותיה (Jeremiah 50:15) and אושיא יחיטו (Ezra 4:12), and Rabbenu Hai Gaon, of blessed memory, said that it is from the root אש, as though it were התחררו, and the Gaon [Saadia], of blessed memory, said that it is from אש and the meaning is 'they were kindled,' like the meaning of והיה בלבי כאש בוערת (Jeremiah 20:9), and they answered this: upon the heart."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {0 "The bracketed [צ\"ל התחררו] is a scribal correction noted in the source; translated as התחררו per the correction. 'They answered this: upon the heart' is hyper-literal for והשיבו זאת על לב, reflecting an abrupt, possibly truncated phrase; the subject of 'they' is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:26.240768594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}